
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We got a nice surprise from Apple this morning with <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/08/apple-introduces-new-mac-studio-with-m5-max-and-m5-ultra/">some new Macs</a>. Those of you waiting for that M5 Ultra Mac Studio are finally going to get your wish. You can get the <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/08/apple-introduces-m6-and-m5-ultra-for-a-big-leap-in-performance-and-ai-compute/">M5 Ultra with up to 36 CPU cores and up to 80 GPU cores</a>. Interestingly, memory tops out at 512 GB. That&#8217;s the same ceiling the M3 Ultra had, and it&#8217;s the configuration <a href="https://www.macsparky.com/blog/2026/03/apple-drops-512gb-ram-option-on-m3-ultra-mac-studio/">Apple dropped back in March</a>. <a href="https://www.tomsguide.com/computing/ram-price-crisis-2026-everything-you-need-to-know">There&#8217;s no mystery why</a>. The M5 Ultra starts at $5,500, up from the $4,000 entry price for the M3 when it launched. Again, no surprise.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">If your needs are more modest, the Mac mini also got updated to <a href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/08/apple-unveils-a-more-powerful-mac-mini-featuring-the-all-new-m6-and-m5-pro/">M6 and M5 Pro variants</a>. That&#8217;s right, we can now buy an M6 Mac.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The mini also <a href="https://www.macworld.com/article/3220063/apple-launches-new-m6-mac-mini-with-another-price-hike.html">took a price hike</a>. The base model is $899 now, up from $599 last fall and $699 since June. I&#8217;m glad Apple released these things. I expect the AI gang will buy them like hotcakes.</p>
